  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: A few bands of mainly light rain showers will \noccur across the North-central Mountains, Middle Susq Valley \nand Western Poconos today as low pressure moves slowly along the\nsouthern New England coast. Otherwise, expect a drying trend to\nwrap up the week.\n\nAnother, relatively weak and compact. mid-upr level vort max (or\ntwo) will be moving south across the eastern part of the CWA \ntoday - on the back side of a slowly departing mid/upper level \nlow. These features will bring a few relatively narrow bands of\nlight to briefly mdt rain showers (and perhaps a low-topped tsra\nthis afternoon) to our far eastern CWA - East of a KIPT to KMUI\nline. \n\nAcross the remainder of Central PA and the Western Alleghenies,\na northerly 850 mb flow (~25 kft) with temps averaging around\n+13C will be slightly under the threshold for Lake Effect \nclouds/showers, considering Lake Ontario and Lake Erie temps in \nthe low to mid 70s. So, cloud cover in this part of the state \nshould be flat and scattered. \n \nExpect dry conditions for Friday and Saturday with sfc dewpoints\nsliding by a few deg F. Chances for showers and thunderstorms \nincrease Saturday night into Sunday ahead of an approaching \nshortwave, but there are still timing differences regarding this\nfeature.",
